.TH FCNTL_PTR 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
fcntl_ptr \- control a file descriptor with a pointer argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.B int fcntl_ptr(int descriptor, int command, void* argument);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Performs a Linux F_* command that takes a pointer, including F_GETLK,
F_SETLK and F_SETLKW.  The supplied struct flock uses the Linux x86\-64 layout.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the command result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fcntl (3crunch),
.BR fcntl (2)
